  <p class="note-line">
    India's own hiring data backs the left column up independent of AI hype: fresher hiring across major
    IT services firms reportedly fell from roughly 600,000 in FY22 to around 120,000 by FY25 — a drop
    driven by revenue and margin pressure as much as by AI, but the two forces point the same direction.
    Fewer junior hands are needed to produce the same output when senior engineers, and AI tools, absorb
    more of the simplest work.
  </p>

  <p>
    This is not a reason to avoid CS. It is a reason to be specific about which layer of the work you
