      <ul>
        <li>Which large companies' first-round filters you clear automatically.</li>
        <li>How much you may need to lean on projects and shipped proof instead of pedigree.</li>
        <li>Whether the two-stage-competition tracks (quant, top-product-company ladders) stay realistic without a major profile change.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">What it does not decide alone</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Your ability to build and ship real projects in AI/ML, cloud, cybersecurity, or your own product.</li>
        <li>Your ability to land clients directly for a consulting practice, where a transcript rarely comes up.</li>
        <li>Your long-term ceiling once you build a genuine skill portfolio and visible proof of work.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    The most degree-agnostic tracks on this map — general software development, cybersecurity, cloud
    work, and your own SaaS or consulting practice — are also the ones where a strong project or a real
    client outcome can outweigh a weaker-brand college fastest.
  </p>

